Problem - Search in Rotated Sorted Array (Leetcode = 33)

Aim - Given the array nums after the possible rotation and an integer target, return the index of target if it is in nums, or -1 if it is not in nums.

Algorithm -
Algorithm: Search in Rotated Sorted Array

1. Start.
2. Initialize low = 0 and high = length(nums) - 1.
3. Repeat while low <= high.
4. Calculate mid = low + (high - low) // 2.
5. If nums[mid] == target, return mid.
6. If nums[low] <= nums[mid], then the left half is sorted.
7. If target >= nums[low] and target < nums[mid], set high = mid - 1.
8. Otherwise, set low = mid + 1.
9. Else, the right half is sorted.
10. If target > nums[mid] and target <= nums[high], set low = mid + 1.
11. Otherwise, set high = mid - 1.
12. Repeat Steps 3 to 11 until the target is found or the search space becomes empty.
13. If the target is not found, return -1.
14. Stop.

Code - 
class Solution(object):
    def search(self, nums, target):
        low = 0
        high = len(nums) - 1

        while low <= high:
            mid = low + (high - low) // 2

            if nums[mid] == target:
                return mid

            if nums[low] <= nums[mid]:
                if nums[low] <= target < nums[mid]:
                    high = mid - 1
                else:
                    low = mid + 1

            else:
                if nums[mid] < target <= nums[high]:
                    low = mid + 1
                else:
                    high = mid - 1

        return -1

